\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The same 60 users and venues, seated two ways. Each line joins a user's home to their table's venue. Random seating sends people back and forth across the Bay; Model B keeps most tables on one side and cuts the average trip from 54 to 22 minutes, raises average satisfaction $p$ from 4.9 to 5.9, more than doubles average pair compatibility $q_{ij}$, and seats all 60 users instead of 57.}}{2}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
